# Code & Markdown Style Rules

## 1. No Emojis Policy

- **CRITICAL**: Never include emojis (pictographs, smileys, symbols, or other colored icons/glyphs) in any file in this repository.
- This applies universally across all file types:
  - Source code (`.js`, `.py`, `.html`, `.css`, etc.)
  - Configuration and metadata files (`.json`, `.yaml`, `.toml`, etc.)
  - Markdown and documentation files (`README.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/*.md`, `data/theses/*.md`, etc.)
  - Rule files, comments, docstrings, and commit messages.
- All headings, bullet points, callouts, and summaries must use clean text and standard ASCII symbols only.

## 2. No Superfluous Horizontal Rules (`---`)

- Do not use standalone horizontal rule dividers (`---`) between sections in Markdown documents.
- Use clean, structured Markdown header hierarchies (`#`, `##`, `###`, `####`) and single blank lines for visual organization.
- Note: Valid YAML frontmatter delimiters at the start of rule/metadata files (e.g. `.mdc`) and table syntax (e.g. `| :--- |`) are permitted.

